## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/lib/network/network_session_manager.dart | ⚠️ important the refresh fence is not cleared on dev sign in — signin resets sessionexpired but leaves the fence producing a sticky healthy looking but dead state completesignin this line refreshexpiredaccount success signout and walletexternallyupdated all clear refreshrejectedaccount but signin network session manager dart 448 460 only sets sessionexpired false — the pr s own fix contract says the fence lifts on an explicit sign in and the dev login form is a reachable always rendered expansiontile in the production sign in dialog sign in dialog dart builddevelopersection the broken observable sequence on that path 1 wallet account s refresh is authoritatively rejected 400 401 403 → fence set jwt null 2 user signs in via the dev login form → signin succeeds jwt set sessionexpired false the fence stays 3 every later accountclient → ensurefreshjwt → account null → refreshrejected account → null silently — the fence branch never re asserts sessionexpired the devices connector s onmanagerchanged fires start hasjwt now true and immediately lands signedout the inbox throws networkinboxunavailableexception result the ui shows a signed in healthy shell hasjwt true sessionexpired false — the expired session note and sign in affordance are gone from the networks dialog while all account bound surfaces stay permanently dead before this change the failing refresh re asserted sessionexpired true on the next read so the recovery path stayed visible the new fence short circuit is what makes the stale false state sticky — the interaction of the new fence with the untouched signin is the regression suggested fix one line mirroring completesignin dart future void signin required string login required string password async jwt token accountlogin login refreshrejectedaccount null a fresh explicit credential lifts the fence sessionexpired false notifylisteners await syncaccountnetworks clearing the fence restores honesty the next account read re attempts refresh once re fences on 401 and re asserts sessionexpired true one request no loop alternatively additionally the fence branch in ensurefreshjwt could re assert sessionexpired true before returning null to keep the fenced ⇒ expired observed invariant under any flag reset |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

