## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/lib/services/flutter_session_manager.dart | ⚠️ important boot resume still reads only the new app owned root — pre upgrade sessions are visible in the sidebar but never resumed at boot this hunk s root move fixes the listing side of the ticket listacrossroots now merges app owned storage a still mounted legacy root defaultsessionsrootforenv moves writes to appstoragecwd sessions but the boot resume consumers still scan the manager s single repo root only createorresumesession flutter session manager dart 966 1044 resolves the resume target via readlastactiveid cachedlist await repo list and passes that same single root cache to findreusablesession the last active marker itself is root local lastactivepath sessionsroot lastactivefile so it moved with the root too on a device upgrading with a project still mounted the exact build339 scenario this pr targets sessions live under sessioncwd sessions legacy while the new app owned root starts empty → first boot logs last active … is gone 0 persisted and mints a fresh session nothing is lost the merged sidebar shows the legacy sessions but when the user opens a legacy session from the sidebar rememberactive writes its id into the new root marker — and the next boot still cannot resolve it repo list is app root only falls through to picking reusable and silently resumes the app root session instead of the conversation the user actually left the documented continuity contract the last active session wins over the newest file — reopen the conversation they actually left stays broken for every legacy root session the pr s device verification doesn t exercise this path the nov 10 duo ledgers were copied into the app owned root manually which masks the gap suggested fix drive the boot path off the same merged candidates — listacrossroots or allsessionrootsforenv inside createorresumesession findreusablesession — and consider migrating the root local last active marker once when a legacy root is detected opening and driving legacy sessions already works absolute metadata path sessionfile metadata path so this is a resume source fix no data movement needed escalation note if boot continuity for pre upgrade sessions is considered part of the ac preserve session history raise this to 🚨 blocking ⚠️ assumes the primary complaint history vanishing from the list on mount unmount as satisfied |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

